      "choice_deviation_redundancy_check": {
        "sentence": "Choice_Deviation is exactly abs(Signed_Deviation), so it adds no information in PRINCIPLE once Signed_Deviation is present -- tested directly rather than assumed: dropping Choice_Deviation while keeping Signed_Deviation changes K-Means ARI from 0.851 to 0.697 (delta=-0.154) and HMM ARI from 0.472 to 0.278 (delta=-0.193), with Left/Right Bias recall at {'Left Bias': 0.9088471849865952, 'Right Bias': 0.9540942928039702} -- at least one delta is non-trivial (>= 0.05), so Choice_Deviation is NOT simply redundant in practice, despite being a deterministic function of Signed_Deviation in principle -- see the exact deltas above rather than assuming redundancy.",
